; expect 42
; A polymorphic callee's placeholder is pinned through the SHAPE of
; its parameter: `applyf :: (-> (-> a b) a b)` applied to `inc`, whose
; type is `(-> Int Int)`, pins `a` and `b` to `Int` from the arrow's
; two halves, so the result is an `Int` the arithmetic below can use.
; Until 2026-08-21 only a BARE placeholder parameter was pinned
; (`pinArg`), so a higher-order call answered a placeholder and
; `(+ (applyf inc 41) 1)` was refused with AX3025 when printed and
; typed as a variable everywhere else (`pinShape`).
;
; 41 + 1 = 42.
(:: applyf (-> (-> a b) a b))

(fn (applyf f x) (f x))

(:: inc (-> Int Int))

(fn (inc n) (+ n 1))

(:: twice (-> (-> a a) a a))

(fn (twice f x) (f (f x)))

(:: main Int)

(fn (main) (+ (applyf inc 39) (twice inc 0)))
